In a standard 5‑card poker hand drawn from a 52‑card deck, the probability of being dealt a **full house** (three cards of one rank plus two cards of another rank) is:

\[
P(\text{Full House})=\frac{\binom{13}{1}\binom{4}{3}\;\times\;\binom{12}{1}\binom{4}{2}}{\binom{52}{5}}
   =\frac{13\times4 \times 12\times6}{2\,598\,960}
   =\frac{3\,744}{2\,598\,960}
   =\frac{6}{4\,165}\approx 0.00144058
\]

So there’s roughly a **0.144 % chance** (about 1 in 694) of drawing a full house in a random 5‑card hand.
